ents. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289619 1113 #uuid "6de83420-f104-50fe-910c-fdae718dbe46" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289619 1145 "We divide the interval of integration into $4$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,-3],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-3,-1],$ the line segment for $x\\in (-1,1),$ and the line segment for $x\\in [1,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-5}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{4}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,-3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,-1].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-1,1).$ The corresponding region is a square, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,4].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{4}=-4.5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}-{A}_{4} \\\\  & =2-2+4-4.5 \\\\  & =-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289621 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289622 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289623 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289624 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289625 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1041 "selection" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289623 13194139534463 true] [17592186289620 1110 #uuid "e0794a0c-f2fc-52b6-a93c-ad4d6e084890" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289621 1034 "0.5" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534463 true] [17592186289621 1111 #uuid "e5b44619-3959-5f1b-b5b5-a9e1aeda34c4" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289622 1034 "-1.5" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534463 true] [17592186289622 1111 #uuid "16b2bfbd-c1bc-52e0-9629-57da1dcc0692" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289623 1034 "-0.5" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534463 true] [17592186289623 1111 #uuid "f663f1be-0479-5f30-af59-c5100d945044" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289624 1034 "1" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534463 true] [17592186289624 1111 #uuid "260baf42-ce8f-537f-9ab8-b6a551cc96f6" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289625 1034 "-1" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534463 true] [17592186289625 1111 #uuid "f8e5f62a-3349-5ba3-a859-45d83a02dc8a" 13194139534463 true] [17592186289626 1017 #edb/ref 17592186289627 13194139534463 true]